{"id": "EUVD-2026-95904", "enisaUuid": "d464c477-92a9-3967-95e9-0fad5c0a38fc", "description": "LobsterAI 2026.5.27 through 2026.9.23 contains an external control of file path vulnerability in the skills:delete IPC handler that trusts the openclawSourceDir value from a skill's _meta.json during uninstall. Attackers who convince a user to install a crafted skill can make uninstallation recursively delete arbitrary user-writable directories, such as the home directory, since the security scanner never inspects _meta.json.", "datePublished": "2026-10-09T16:04:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T01:59:13", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/netease-youdao/LobsterAI/issues/2793", "https://github.com/netease-youdao/LobsterAI/blob/791a352dee3b3d8c6f64edcaf229ce474a68f6c5/src/main/ipcHandlers/skills/handlers.ts#L60-L78", "https://github.com/netease-youdao/LobsterAI/commit/82fdfe10d1b85d0ff734aa720e18c866b4be2406", "https://github.com/netease-youdao/LobsterAI", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/lobsterai-2026.5.27-through-2026.9.23-arbitrary-directory-deletion-via-skill-meta-json"], "aliases": ["GHSA-pwqg-g4m5-54gf", "CVE-2026-108156"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9657828d-6044-35db-aa28-5172519a0041", "product": {"name": "LobsterAI", "vendor": {"name": "netease-youdao"}}, "product_version": "2026.5.27 \u22642026.9.23"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bcbe2023-86c8-3fff-b636-02e85e1f6b58", "vendor": {"name": "netease-youdao"}}], "isExploited": false}